# What this file is for: the diffs GitHub shows for this repository, and the
# language it reports.
#
# Measured, before any of the rules below (tracked bytes):
#
#   Go              7,067,952   820 files
#   TSX             1,414,659   198
#   TS              1,395,084   165
#   Markdown          906,109   113
#   YAML              885,326    87
#   JSON              271,155    20
#   SQL               216,681    44
#   Proto             185,956    33
#   Shell             170,723    33
#   PowerShell         24,133     4
#
# The two attributes do different things, which decides most of what is below:
# linguist-generated excludes from stats AND hides in diffs, while
# linguist-vendored only excludes from stats.
#
# Every rule was checked against Linguist's own lib/linguist/generated.rb
# rather than assumed, because the redundant rule and the missing one look
# identical from here — both leave a file rendered the way it already was.

# ─── Generated TypeScript from protobuf ──────────────────────────────────
# 753 KB across 36 files, and the one rule here with a real effect on review:
# a regenerated stub set otherwise arrives as the largest diff in the pull
# request and buries the hand-written change beside it.
#
# Linguist does NOT catch these on its own, and that is the whole reason the
# rule exists. generated_typescript_protocol_buffer? tests `lines[0]` for the
# exact string "Code generated by protoc-gen-ts_proto. DO NOT EDIT." — we
# generate with protoc-gen-es, which writes "@generated by protoc-gen-es"
# instead, and for the vendored halves of the tree (buf/validate, google/api,
# google/rpc) that marker sits on line 15 behind an upstream licence header
# where nothing would look for it anyway.
frontend/src/gen/** linguist-generated=true

# ─── Generated: the module checksum files ────────────────────────────────
# 52 KB over backend/go.sum and capability/go.sum, reviewed as "the lock
# moved" and never line by line.
#
# Not redundant: generated.rb knows the JavaScript and Python lockfiles —
# pnpm_lock? and npm_shrinkwrap_or_package_lock? among them — and go.sum
# appears nowhere in it.
#
# go.mod is deliberately absent. It is hand-edited, and collapsing it would
# hide exactly the line a reviewer needs to see.
**/go.sum linguist-generated=true

# ─── Not this repository's language ──────────────────────────────────────
# A Homebrew bundle, which Linguist reads as Ruby because languages.yml claims
# the filename. It is ALL of the Ruby GitHub reports, for a repository that
# contains none.
#
# `-linguist-detectable` rather than -generated or -vendored, because both of
# those would be untrue: it is hand-written and a reviewer should see it in
# full. The attribute says only "do not count this as a language".
Brewfile -linguist-detectable

# ─── Vendored tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spec-Kit's own scripts and templates, 192 KB, including every one of the
# four PowerShell files in the tree — a language this project does not
# otherwise use and does not want on its bar. The directory is upstream's,
# carried here so a feature plan resolves offline.

# The shared Task library's module bodies, 159 KB, committed so TASK_OFFLINE=1
# resolves every include from this repository instead of cloning. They are
# another repository's source, kept verbatim — see .gitignore for why the
# checksums travel with them.
.task/remote/** linguist-vendored=true

# ─── Deliberately not marked ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every generated Go file: the protobuf messages, the Connect stubs and the
# sqlc bindings, 1.68 MB in all. generated_go? reads `lines.first(40)` for
# `^// Code generated .*`, and all three generators write that on line 1
# ("protoc-gen-go", "protoc-gen-connect-go", "sqlc"), so Linguist already
# excludes and collapses them. sqlc/generate.go is the one hand-written file
# in that directory and correctly keeps its diff — it has no such header.
#
# frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml and package-lock.json: generated.rb matches both by
# filename already.
#
# The .proto files stay detectable on purpose. They are the contract, written
# and reviewed here, and 186 KB of Protocol Buffers is an honest description
# of what this repository is.
#
# migrations/*.sql likewise: hand-written, and the schema is the thing a
# reviewer most needs to read line by line.

# ─── Version for a source archive ────────────────────────────────────────
# git archive (and a GitHub tarball of a tag) fills in .git_archival.txt, so
# the Python SDK built from it without git still knows its sdk/go/v* version.
.git_archival.txt export-subst
